-- allium: 3
--
-- nixtune: a declarative network music player. A NixOS module
-- (services.nixtune.*) plus a PureScript (Halogen) page, built as a
-- public flake and consumed by the neoblade-config fleet as one input
-- and one row. A clean reimplementation of what moOde audio player
-- does, with none of moOde's code, none of its name, and none of its
-- runtime configuration machinery.
--
-- STATE OF THE WORLD, 2026-10-30, 03:00. The hardware works. This
-- revision records how it got there and specifies the next thing,
-- the page as a shared player for a room.
--
--   Repositories (both on winsmuth; neither pushed):
--     ~/git/nixtune             the public flake: flake.nix, nix/module/
--                               {default,hardware,mpd,library,ui,airplay,
--                               upnp}.nix, packages/upmpdcli.nix,
--                               packages/nixtune-web/. Its flake.lock pins
--                               nixpkgs to 6510408d (KnownIssue
--                               purescript_segfault). A devShell carries
--                               spago from purescript-overlay for editing
--                               the lock; consumers never evaluate it.
--     ~/neoblade-config         the fleet. Input `nixtune` =
--                               git+file:///home/bismuth/git/nixtune,
--                               nixpkgs following. Adapter role
--                               modules/system/player.nix; rows `nixtune`
--                               (aarch64, Pi) and `nixtune-vm` (x86 QEMU);
--                               facts in hosts/nixtune.nix and
--                               hosts/nixtune-vm.nix. deployAddr is the
--                               NAME nixtune.lan, which the router's DNS
--                               gives to whichever interface holds the
--                               lease; the earlier plan of one reserved
--                               address per MAC was abandoned because the
--                               wired and wireless MACs differ.
--
--   Verified on the Pi (Raspberry Pi 5 Model B Rev 1.1, HiFiBerry DAC2
--   HD, Samsung 128 GB card):
--     - Boots the generic aarch64 SD image with U-Boot chainloaded by the
--       GPU firmware (hardware.raspberry-pi.firmware.uboot.enable, set
--       by the module when nixos-hardware's Pi options are present).
--     - The DAC appears as ALSA card sndrpihifiberry with mixer control
--       DAC; MPD plays GBH 89.7 through it with hardware volume. The
--       overlay arrives as a config.txt dtoverlay line rendered by
--       nixos-hardware; the compatible-string rewrite for the generation
--       DTB path is kept but unused on this boot path.
--     - mpd, nixtune-websocket, nginx, shairport-sync active; no failed
--       units after the ordering fix in library.nix and auto_update off.
--     - /srv/music mounts from the Synology; the rescan timer runs two
--       minutes after boot and daily.
--     - Wifi: secrets/nixtune.yaml holds user-password and wifi-psk
--       (PSK=... form), the profile PissiNet-5G is written from the sops
--       path, and the cable has come out.
--   Lessons that cost a night, written down so they are not paid twice:
--     - nixpkgs' online first-boot resize of the ext4 root (sd-image's
--       expandOnBoot) corrupted directory blocks across the nixpkgs
--       source in the store; the image file was clean (e2fsck -fn on a
--       loop device), the card stored the image byte for byte (sha256
--       over the image length, modulo the few bytes a desktop automount
--       writes), and a card grown OFFLINE on winsmuth (sfdisk, e2fsck,
--       resize2fs) booted clean. KnownIssue sd_resize below.
--     - MPD's auto_update installs inotify watches over the whole tree
--       on its main thread before notifying systemd; on a vast NFS
--       library this exceeded the start timeout. inotify never fires for
--       NFS writes anyway. Off; a timer runs `mpc update`.
--     - A host reads capabilities.json once at page load; a stale tab
--       keeps a stale station list.
--     - e2fsprogs and parted are not on winsmuth; every tool outside
--       coreutils and util-linux is invoked through `nix shell`.
--
-- Design decisions that shape this spec:
--
--   1. The only source of configuration is the Nix declaration. No
--      settings database, no settings page, no daemon that rewrites
--      /etc or /boot.
--   2. Every optional capability is a sub-option with an enable flag
--      defaulting to false; a disabled one contributes nothing.
--   3. The page is a Halogen single page application that speaks the
--      MPD protocol itself over websockets bridged by websocat. There is
--      no backend code on the Pi, and decision 8 below is made under
--      that constraint.
--   4. No over the air updates. Updates arrive only as new generations.
--   5. The root filesystem is NOT ephemeral yet; the module publishes
--      persistPaths and the fleet adapter maps it into the manifest.
--   6. Two layers, one boundary: the public module knows no fleet; the
--      adapter maps fleet facts into its options.
--   7. Maintenance is `nix flake update` on an update branch, CI, merge.
--
-- Decisions taken 2026-10-30 (the page as a room's player, from a
-- questionnaire):
--   8. ROLES WITHOUT A BACKEND. Two pages from one bundle: the guest
--      page at / and the host page at /host. The QR code on the host
--      page encodes the guest URL. There is no token and no rotation:
--      a rotating token needs something on the Pi that issues and
--      checks it, and the decision was to keep the Pi free of
--      application servers rather than add one for this. The host URL
--      is a path known to the host; it is not a secret in any strong
--      sense. THE CONSEQUENCE, stated plainly: role limits are enforced
--      by the page, not by the Pi. Both pages reach the same websocket,
--      and a guest who opens a browser console can send any MPD command.
--      This is accepted for a LAN of invited people. A filtering proxy
--      between websocat and MPD is the upgrade path if that stops being
--      acceptable; it is an open question, not a plan.
--   9. GUESTS APPEND ONLY. A guest sees now playing (read-only) and the
--      library (browse first; search secondary), and may add a track or
--      a folder to the END of the queue. Guests do not see the queue, do
--      not remove or reorder, do not skip, do not touch transport or
--      volume. The host page has everything the page has today plus the
--      QR, the attribution column and the scan indicator.
--  10. GUEST IDENTITY IS A NICKNAME PER DEVICE, generated by the page on
--      first visit (adjective plus animal, from word lists in the
--      bundle), kept in that browser's localStorage, never prompted for.
--      Attribution lives in MPD stickers: on append the page sets
--      sticker song <uri> nixtune.added_by <nickname>; the host's queue
--      view reads it back. Stickers are per URI, not per queue entry,
--      so the same file added twice shows the latest adder; accepted.
--  11. LIBRARY = Music/ ONLY. library.export points at
--      /volume2/music/Music; audiobooks, ringtones and the rename
--      queues are outside MPD's world. The first scan runs for days in
--      the background on the Pi; the page shows a quiet indicator (song
--      count and "scanning") in the header until updating_db clears,
--      and everything already scanned is browsable meanwhile.
--  12. NO COVER ART in this release; text only.
--  13. THE QR IS BUILT BY NIX: qrencode renders the guest URL
--      (services.nixtune.ui.publicUrl, default http://<hostname>.lan/)
--      to qr.svg in the closure, served beside the page. No QR library
--      in the bundle, nothing generated at runtime.
--
-- Earlier decisions still in force: AirPlay on, UPnP off until upmpdcli
-- builds, DSP out of scope, SD card on oracle's boot path, hardware
-- profile from the datasheet, the staged scope of 2026-10-28 (public
-- release, then arbiter and renderers, then the long tail).

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Given
------------------------------------------------------------

given {
    host: HostDeclaration
    player: Player
    output: OutputDevice
    module_repo: ProjectRepository
    fleet_repo: FleetConfig
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- External Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

external entity FleetConfig {
    repo_path: String
    input_url: String
    adapter_module: String
    build_command: String
}

-- A browser on the LAN. Identity is a nickname the page made up and
-- stored in that browser; nothing on the Pi knows who anyone is.
external entity Client {
    address: String
    on_lan: Boolean
    nickname: String?
}

external entity Nas {
    address: String
    export: String
    allows: Set<String>
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

value SystemClosure {
    store_path: String
    flake_revision: String
}

value Track {
    uri: String
    title: String?
    artist: String?
    album: String?
    duration: Duration?
}

-- What nix/module/ui.nix writes to capabilities.json at build time.
value Capabilities {
    hostname: String
    profile: String
    output_kind: alsa | null_output
    card: String?
    mixer: String?
    modules: Set<ModuleKind>
    library: Boolean
    stations: List<RadioStation>
    websocket_path: String
    max_volume: Integer
    public_url: String
    host_path: String
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

contract PlayerModule {
    evaluate: (declaration: HostDeclaration) -> SystemClosure

    @invariant Purity
        -- Evaluation reads only the Nix declaration and pinned inputs.
        -- The page's dependencies are fixed-output fetches checked
        -- against spago.lock; nothing fetches during evaluation.

    @invariant Determinism
        -- Same declaration, same lock, same closure.

    @invariant LazyModules
        -- A disabled sub-option contributes nothing to the closure.

    @invariant NoRuntimeConfiguration
        -- Nothing in the closure writes to /etc, /boot or the store at
        -- runtime. The nickname and the host path are browser-side.

    @invariant FleetAgnostic
        -- The module references only nixpkgs' option tree, its own
        -- services.nixtune.*, and, when present, nixos-hardware's
        -- hardware.raspberry-pi.* (guarded by `options.hardware ?
        -- raspberry-pi`, with optionalAttrs rather than mkIf so a host
        -- without those options never sees the attribute path).

    @guidance
        -- Options, as implemented plus the two this revision adds:
        --   enable
        --   hardware.profile            "pi5-dac2hd" | "none"
        --   library.export              "host:/path" or null
        --   wifi.ssid, wifi.pskFile
        --   mpd.port, mpd.exposeOnLan, mpd.maxVolume
        --   radio.stations
        --   ui.enable, ui.package, ui.port
        --   ui.publicUrl                NEW: what the QR encodes; default
        --                               "http://<hostname>.lan/"
        --   ui.hostPath                 NEW: default "/host"
        --   arbitration.resumeAfterRenderer
        --   renderers.airplay.{enable,name}
        --   renderers.upnp.{enable,friendlyName,package}
        --   persistPaths (read-only), output.* (internal)
        -- On a Pi: firmware.uboot.enable = true and the DAC overlay as a
        -- config.txt line (hardware.nix).
}

contract MpdBridge {
    status: () -> PlayerStatus
    command: (command: String) -> PlayerStatus
    capabilities: () -> Capabilities

    @invariant ReadOnlySystem
        -- Only the MPD protocol passes; the capability file is static.

    @invariant LanOnly
        -- nginx on 0.0.0.0:<ui.port>; websocat and MPD on loopback.

    @invariant NoRoleEnforcement
        -- The bridge does not know which page a socket came from. Role
        -- limits are the page's (decision 8).

    @guidance
        -- websocat -t -E ws-l:127.0.0.1:8600 tcp:127.0.0.1:<mpd.port> as
        -- nixtune-websocket.service; nginx /ws proxies it; the page
        -- holds one command socket with a reply queue and one idle
        -- socket. Both pages use the same two sockets.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

enum ModuleKind {
    mpd
    | airplay
    | upnp_renderer
    | spotify_connect
    | squeezelite
    | bluetooth
    | web_ui
}

enum Role { host | guest }

enum NetworkKind { wired | wifi }

enum PlaybackState { playing | paused | stopped }

enum ScanState { never_scanned | scanning | scanned }

enum ReleaseStep { pi_plays | room_page | public_release | arbiter_and_renderers | long_tail }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

entity HardwareProfile {
    name: String
    board: String
    dac_overlay: String?
    card: String?
    mixer_control: String?
    hardware_volume: Boolean
    needs_pi_kernel: Boolean
}

entity HostDeclaration {
    hostname: String
    hardware: HardwareProfile
    network: NetworkKind
    ssid: String?
    psk_file: String?
    library_export: String?
    public_url: String
    host_path: String
    fleet: FleetConfig?

    modules: ModuleDeclaration with host = this
    enabled_modules: modules where enabled = true
    renderers: modules where kind in {airplay, upnp_renderer, spotify_connect, squeezelite, bluetooth}
    enabled_renderers: renderers where enabled = true

    radio_stations: RadioStation with host = this
    persisted_paths: PersistedPath with host = this
    generations: Generation with host = this
    secrets: SecretsFile? with host = this

    booted_generation: generations where status = booted
    capabilities: enabled_modules -> kind
    has_core: modules.any(m => m.kind = mpd and m.enabled)
    has_ui: modules.any(m => m.kind = web_ui and m.enabled)
    wifi_configured: ssid != null and psk_file != null

    invariant CoreIsMandatory {
        has_core
    }

    invariant OneBootedGeneration {
        booted_generation.count <= 1
    }

    invariant AirplayNeedsCard {
        enabled_renderers.any(r => r.kind = airplay) implies hardware.card != null
    }

    invariant HostPathIsNotRoot {
        host_path != "/"
    }

    @guidance
        -- The fleet member: hostname nixtune, deployAddr nixtune.lan,
        -- pi5-dac2hd, ssid PissiNet-5G, library export
        -- 192.168.8.110:/volume2/music/Music (roles.player.musicExport =
        -- "/volume2/music/Music" in hosts/nixtune.nix), AirPlay on as
        -- "nixtune", UPnP off, stations GBH 89.7 and CRB Classical 99.5,
        -- public_url http://nixtune.lan/, host_path /host.
}

entity ModuleDeclaration {
    host: HostDeclaration
    kind: ModuleKind
    enabled: Boolean
    state: inactive | active
    is_renderer: kind in {airplay, upnp_renderer, spotify_connect, squeezelite, bluetooth}

    invariant DisabledModulesAreInactive {
        not enabled implies state = inactive
    }
}

entity SecretsFile {
    host: HostDeclaration
    path: String
    has_user_password: Boolean
    has_wifi_psk: Boolean

    @guidance
        -- Created without an editor session: the hash from mkpasswd and
        -- the passphrase are staged in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR (RAM), their
        -- lengths checked (a yescrypt hash is 73 characters; sops
        -- rejects a YAML null for a key it must install), encrypted with
        -- `sops --encrypt --filename-override secrets/<host>.yaml`, and
        -- the staging file removed. Verification prints lengths and
        -- prefixes, never values.
}

entity OutputDevice {
    host: HostDeclaration
    profile: HardwareProfile
    owner: ModuleDeclaration?
    volume: Integer

    invariant VolumeInRange {
        volume >= 0 and volume <= 100
    }

    invariant OwnerIsEnabled {
        owner != null implies owner.enabled
    }
}

entity Player {
    host: HostDeclaration
    state: PlaybackState
    current: QueueEntry?
    queue: List<QueueEntry>
    scan: ScanState
    song_count: Integer
    last_error: String?
    sessions: Session with player = this
    open_sessions: sessions where status = open
}

-- A track in the queue with who put it there. The attribution is an
-- MPD sticker on the track's URI (nixtune.added_by); null for tracks
-- the host queued or that predate the sticker.
entity QueueEntry {
    position: Integer
    track: Track
    added_by: String?
}

value PlayerStatus {
    state: PlaybackState
    current: QueueEntry?
    volume: Integer?
    queue_length: Integer
    scan: ScanState
    song_count: Integer
    capabilities: Set<ModuleKind>
}

entity Session {
    player: Player
    client: Client
    role: Role
    status: open | closed
    opened_at: Timestamp

    invariant GuestsAreNamed {
        role = guest implies client.nickname != null
    }
}

entity RadioStation {
    host: HostDeclaration
    name: String
    stream_url: String
    verified: Boolean
}

entity PersistedPath {
    host: HostDeclaration
    path: String
}

entity Generation {
    host: HostDeclaration
    closure: SystemClosure
    status: built | booted | previous | discarded
    built_at: Timestamp

    transitions status {
        built -> booted
        built -> discarded
        booted -> previous
        previous -> booted
        previous -> discarded
        terminal: discarded
    }
}

entity ProjectRepository {
    path: String
    public_url: String?
    main_revision: String
    nixpkgs_pin: String
    runs: UpdateRun with repo = this
    open_runs: runs where status in {opened, checked}
    issues: KnownIssue with repo = this

    invariant OneUpdateRunAtATime {
        open_runs.count <= 1
    }
}

entity UpdateRun {
    repo: ProjectRepository
    branch: String
    status: opened | checked | merged | abandoned
    ci_passed: Boolean
    lock_revision: String

    transitions status {
        opened -> checked
        opened -> abandoned
        checked -> merged
        checked -> abandoned
        terminal: merged, abandoned
    }
}

entity KnownIssue {
    repo: ProjectRepository
    name: String
    status: open | closed
    effect: String
    closes_when: String
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    mpd_port: Integer = 6600
    ui_port: Integer = 80
    websocket_port: Integer = 8600
    max_volume: Integer = 100
    rescan_after_boot: Duration = 2.minutes
    rescan_every: Duration = 1.day
    resume_mpd_after_renderer: Boolean = true
    current_step: ReleaseStep = room_page
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Defaults
------------------------------------------------------------

default HardwareProfile pi5_dac2hd = {
    name: "Raspberry Pi 5 with HiFiBerry DAC2 HD",
    board: "raspberrypi-5",
    dac_overlay: "hifiberry-dacplushd",
    card: "sndrpihifiberry",
    mixer_control: "DAC",
    hardware_volume: true,
    needs_pi_kernel: true
}

default HardwareProfile none = {
    name: "No sound card (rehearsal)",
    board: "any",
    dac_overlay: null,
    card: null,
    mixer_control: null,
    hardware_volume: false,
    needs_pi_kernel: false
}

default FleetConfig neoblade = {
    repo_path: "/home/bismuth/neoblade-config",
    input_url: "git+file:///home/bismuth/git/nixtune",
    adapter_module: "modules/system/player.nix",
    build_command: "./build boot-native nixtune"
}

default ProjectRepository nixtune = {
    path: "/home/bismuth/git/nixtune",
    public_url: null,
    main_revision: "",
    nixpkgs_pin: "6510408d147d8c5e6d76043e899e9251756f6a75"
}

default KnownIssue sd_resize = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "sd-image's online first-boot resize corrupts the root filesystem",
    status: open,
    effect: "a card that boots straight from the image as built loses directory blocks in the store; the workaround is the offline grow on winsmuth before first boot",
    closes_when: "sdImage.expandOnBoot = false in the nixtune row's extraModules (and oracle's), the offline grow written into the first-boot header of hosts/nixtune.nix, and the cause reported upstream with the e2fsck transcript"
}

default KnownIssue upmpdcli_unbuilt = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "upmpdcli hashes are lib.fakeHash",
    status: open,
    effect: "renderers.upnp cannot be enabled",
    closes_when: "nix build ~/git/nixtune#upmpdcli has been through all three hash errors; versions unverified"
}

default KnownIssue purescript_segfault = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "nixpkgs' prebuilt purs 0.15.15 segfaults on nixos-unstable newer than the pin",
    status: open,
    effect: "the public repo's lock stays on the fleet's nixpkgs revision",
    closes_when: "a newer nixpkgs builds purescript, or the page build switches to a purs built from source"
}

default KnownIssue no_impermanence = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "ext4 root without wipe-on-boot",
    status: open,
    effect: "the fleet's ext4-root warning; persistPaths mapped but inert",
    closes_when: "the rollback cycle has been rehearsed on a Pi and both Pi rows adopt it together"
}

default KnownIssue oracle_uboot = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "oracle's image would not boot if rebuilt",
    status: open,
    effect: "hosts/oracle.nix does not set hardware.raspberry-pi.firmware.uboot.enable; its running install is unaffected",
    closes_when: "the option is added to hosts/oracle.nix in its own fleet commit"
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Boot and generations -----------------------------------------------

rule HostBootsGeneration {
    when: HostBoots(generation)
    requires: generation.status = built
    let current = host.booted_generation
    ensures:
        for g in current:
            g.status = previous
        generation.status = booted
        CoreStarted(host: host)
}

rule OperatorRollsBack {
    when: OperatorRollsBack(operator, generation)
    requires: generation.status = previous
    let current = host.booted_generation
    ensures:
        for g in current:
            g.status = previous
        generation.status = booted
}

rule CoreStartsOnBoot {
    when: CoreStarted(host)
    let core = ModuleDeclaration{host: host, kind: mpd}
    requires: exists core
    requires: core.enabled
    ensures:
        core.state = active
        output.owner = core
        player.state = stopped
        for m in host.enabled_modules where kind != mpd:
            m.state = active

    @guidance
        -- MPD starts after network-online and the library automount,
        -- with auto_update off, so it reports ready to systemd at once
        -- regardless of library size.
}

-- Library scanning ------------------------------------------------------

rule RescanTimerFires {
    when: RescanDue(host)
    requires: host.library_export != null
    requires: player.scan != scanning
    ensures:
        player.scan = scanning
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)

    @guidance
        -- nixtune-library-update.timer: OnBootSec 2min, OnUnitActiveSec
        -- 1d, running `mpc update` as a oneshot. MPD walks the tree in
        -- its update thread; the main loop keeps serving. On an
        -- unchanged tree the walk compares mtimes only.
}

rule ScanProgresses {
    when: MpdDatabaseGrew(player, count)
    requires: player.scan = scanning
    ensures:
        player.song_count = count
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)

    @guidance
        -- The idle socket reports "database" changes as MPD commits
        -- batches; the page re-asks `stats` and shows the count. On the
        -- first scan of Music/ this continues for days; every batch is
        -- browsable as soon as it is committed.
}

rule ScanCompletes {
    when: MpdUpdateFinished(player)
    requires: player.scan = scanning
    ensures:
        player.scan = scanned
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)

    @guidance
        -- `status` loses its updating_db line. MPD writes the database
        -- file to /var/lib/mpd at the end of the job and on shutdown, so
        -- a reboot mid-scan keeps what was committed and the next timer
        -- run resumes from mtimes.
}

-- Sessions and roles ----------------------------------------------------

rule GuestOpensSession {
    when: ClientOpens(client, path)
    requires: client.on_lan
    requires: host.has_ui
    requires: path != host.host_path
    ensures:
        if client.nickname = null:
            client.nickname = GeneratedNickname()
        Session.created(player: player, client: client, role: guest, status: open, opened_at: now)
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)

    @guidance
        -- The guest page is the default page, so the QR encodes
        -- public_url with no path. The nickname is adjective + animal
        -- from two short word lists in the bundle, drawn once and kept
        -- in localStorage; a cleared browser gets a new name.
}

rule HostOpensSession {
    when: ClientOpens(client, path)
    requires: client.on_lan
    requires: host.has_ui
    requires: path = host.host_path
    ensures:
        Session.created(player: player, client: client, role: host, status: open, opened_at: now)
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)

    @guidance
        -- nginx serves the same index.html for / and for host_path
        -- (tryFiles falls through to it); the page reads
        -- window.location.pathname against capabilities.hostPath to
        -- choose the role. No credential. Decision 8 says why.
}

rule SessionCloses {
    when: ClientDisconnects(session)
    requires: session.status = open
    ensures: session.status = closed
}

-- What a guest may do -----------------------------------------------------

rule GuestBrowses {
    when: ClientBrowses(session, path)
    requires: session.status = open
    ensures: LibraryListingDelivered(session: session, path: path)

    @guidance
        -- lsinfo over the command socket, both roles. Browse first: the
        -- tree is the main view, a search box (MPD `search any`) sits
        -- above it on the same view.
}

rule GuestAppends {
    when: ClientAppends(session, uri)
    requires: session.status = open
    requires: session.role = guest
    ensures:
        MpdProtocol.apply(player, "add " + uri)
        MpdProtocol.apply(player, "sticker set song " + uri + " nixtune.added_by " + session.client.nickname)
        player.queue = player.queue + [ { position: player.queue.count, track: Track{uri: uri}, added_by: session.client.nickname } ]
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)

    @guidance
        -- `add` appends by definition; the guest page offers no other
        -- queue command. A folder URI appends its contents in MPD's
        -- order, with one sticker per file. If nothing is playing the
        -- guest page also sends `play`, so a room with a silent player
        -- and a first guest gets music; that is the one transport
        -- command a guest can cause, and only from the stopped state.
}

rule GuestCommandNotOffered {
    when: ClientCommands(session, command)
    requires: session.status = open
    requires: session.role = guest
    requires: command not in {"add", "lsinfo", "search", "status", "currentsong", "stats", "sticker get", "idle"}
    ensures: CommandNotOffered(session: session, command: command)

    @guidance
        -- "Not offered" is exact: the guest page renders no control that
        -- sends these. The websocket would carry them. See decision 8.
}

-- What the host may do --------------------------------------------------

rule HostCommands {
    when: ClientCommands(session, command)
    requires: session.status = open
    requires: session.role = host
    ensures:
        MpdProtocol.apply(player, command)
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)

    @guidance
        -- Everything the page does today: transport, random, repeat,
        -- setvol clamped to maxVolume, clear/add/play for stations and
        -- paths, play <pos>, delete <pos>, load <playlist>, plus
        -- `update` to force a rescan now.
}

rule HostSeesAttribution {
    when: PlayerStatusChanged(player)
    for s in player.open_sessions where role = host:
        ensures: QueueDelivered(session: s, queue: player.queue)

    @guidance
        -- The host queue view shows the nickname beside each entry,
        -- from `sticker get song <uri> nixtune.added_by` per entry,
        -- fetched when the playlist changes and cached per URI in the
        -- page. Now playing shows "added by <nickname>" on both pages.
}

rule HostShowsQr {
    when: HostOpensQr(session)
    requires: session.role = host
    ensures: QrDelivered(session: session, url: host.public_url)

    @guidance
        -- A QR tab on the host page shows /qr.svg full width with the
        -- URL printed under it. qrencode -t SVG at build time in ui.nix,
        -- joined into the static root beside capabilities.json.
}

-- Status fan-out --------------------------------------------------------

rule StatusPushedToSessions {
    when: PlayerStatusChanged(player)
    for s in player.open_sessions:
        ensures: StatusDelivered(session: s, status: {
            state: player.state,
            current: player.current,
            volume: output.volume,
            queue_length: player.queue.count,
            scan: player.scan,
            song_count: player.song_count,
            capabilities: host.capabilities
        })

    @guidance
        -- Both pages keep the idle socket. The guest page shows state,
        -- current track, who added it, and the scan indicator; it hides
        -- volume and the queue.
}

-- Output arbitration (unchanged) ------------------------------------------

rule RendererAcquiresOutput {
    when: RendererStreamStarts(module)
    requires: module.enabled
    requires: module.is_renderer
    requires: module.state = active
    requires: output.owner = null or output.owner.kind = mpd
    ensures:
        if player.state = playing:
            player.state = paused
        output.owner = module
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)
}

rule RendererReleasesOutput {
    when: RendererStreamStops(module)
    requires: output.owner = module
    let core = ModuleDeclaration{host: host, kind: mpd}
    ensures:
        output.owner = core
        if config.resume_mpd_after_renderer and player.state = paused:
            player.state = playing
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)
}

-- Project maintenance ---------------------------------------------------

rule MaintainerOpensUpdateRun {
    when: MaintainerRunsFlakeUpdate(maintainer)
    requires: module_repo.open_runs.count = 0
    ensures:
        UpdateRun.created(repo: module_repo, branch: "update", status: opened, ci_passed: false, lock_revision: "")
}

rule CiChecksUpdateRun {
    when: CiCompletes(run, passed)
    requires: run.status = opened
    ensures:
        run.status = checked
        run.ci_passed = passed
}

rule MaintainerMergesUpdateRun {
    when: MaintainerMerges(maintainer, run)
    requires: run.status = checked
    requires: run.ci_passed
    ensures:
        run.status = merged
        module_repo.main_revision = run.lock_revision
        FleetInputBumped(fleet: fleet_repo, revision: run.lock_revision)
}

rule MaintainerClosesIssue {
    when: IssueFixed(issue, revision)
    requires: issue.status = open
    ensures: issue.status = closed
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant SingleOutputOwner {
    for d in OutputDevices:
        d.owner != null implies d.owner.state = active
}

invariant GuestsNeverRemove {
    -- Over the page's own surface. Not over the websocket (decision 8).
    for s in Sessions where role = guest:
        s.status = open implies not Offered(s, "delete") and not Offered(s, "clear") and not Offered(s, "move")
}

invariant NicknamesAreBrowserState {
    for c in Clients:
        c.nickname != null implies StoredIn(c.nickname, "localStorage")
}

invariant ScanNeverBlocksStart {
    for p in Players:
        p.scan = scanning implies ModuleDeclaration{host: p.host, kind: mpd}.state = active
}

invariant MainIsAlwaysChecked {
    for r in UpdateRuns:
        r.status = merged implies r.ci_passed
}

invariant UpnpOffWhileUnbuilt {
    for h in HostDeclarations:
        upmpdcli_unbuilt.status = open implies not h.enabled_renderers.any(r => r.kind = upnp_renderer)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

actor Guest {
    identified_by: Session where role = guest
}

actor Host {
    identified_by: Session where role = host
}

actor Operator {
    identified_by: Client where on_lan = true
}

actor Maintainer {
    identified_by: Client where on_lan = true
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

surface GuestPage {
    facing guest: Guest

    exposes:
        player.state
        player.current
        player.current.added_by
        player.scan
        player.song_count
        host.hostname
        guest.client.nickname

    provides:
        ClientBrowses(session, path)
        ClientAppends(session, uri)
        ClientDisconnects(session)

    contracts:
        demands MpdBridge

    @guarantee AppendOnlyByConstruction
        -- The guest page contains no control that sends a queue command
        -- other than add (and play from the stopped state). This is a
        -- guarantee about the page, not about the wire.

    @guarantee NoVolumeNoQueue
        -- No volume slider, no queue view, no transport buttons.

    @guidance
        -- Two views: Now playing (title, artist/album, progress, "added
        -- by", the scan indicator in the header, "you are <nickname>" in
        -- the footer) and Library (breadcrumbs, search box, folders and
        -- files, a + on each). Phone-first, dark by default.
}

surface HostPage {
    facing host: Host

    exposes:
        player.state
        player.current
        player.queue
        player.scan
        player.song_count
        player.last_error
        output.volume
        host.public_url
        for m in host.enabled_modules:
            m.kind
        for s in host.radio_stations:
            s.name

    provides:
        ClientCommands(session, command)
        ClientBrowses(session, path)
        HostOpensQr(session)
        ClientDisconnects(session)

    contracts:
        demands MpdBridge

    @guarantee NoSettingsSurface
        -- Hardware, modules, sources and stations are shown, never
        -- edited.

    @guidance
        -- The page as it exists today (Now playing, Queue, Library,
        -- Radio) plus a QR tab, the nickname column in the queue,
        -- "added by" on now playing, the scan indicator, and an Update
        -- button on the Library view that sends `update`.
}

surface FleetDeployment {
    facing operator: Operator

    exposes:
        host.hostname
        host.network
        for g in host.generations:
            g.status
        for i in module_repo.issues where status = open:
            i.name
            i.effect

    provides:
        OperatorRollsBack(operator, generation) when host.generations.any(g => g.status = previous)

    contracts:
        demands PlayerModule

    @guarantee FleetShape
        -- One row, one adapter, two host files; deployAddr is a name.

    @guidance
        -- Day to day: edit hosts/nixtune.nix or ~/git/nixtune, `git add`
        -- there, `nix flake update nixtune`, `./build check`,
        -- `./build deploy-native nixtune`, live with it,
        -- `./build boot-native nixtune`. A fresh card: build the image,
        -- dd, grow OFFLINE (sfdisk, e2fsck -f, resize2fs, e2fsck -fn),
        -- boot on the cable, ssh-to-age, secrets, deploy, boot-native,
        -- unplug.
}

surface CommunityFlake {
    facing adopter: Operator

    exposes:
        module_repo.public_url
        module_repo.nixpkgs_pin
        for i in module_repo.issues where status = open:
            i.name

    contracts:
        demands PlayerModule

    @guarantee StandaloneUse
        -- Import nixosModules.default, set services.nixtune.*, import
        -- nixos-hardware's raspberry-pi-5 for the Pi profile. The flake
        -- template is the public_release step.

    @guidance
        -- AGPLv3 (LICENSE still to be added). No moOde code or name.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred MpdProtocol.apply          -- see: https://mpd.readthedocs.io/en/latest/protocol.html
deferred MpdProtocol.stickers       -- see: the sticker commands in the same document
deferred Firmware.configtxt         -- see: nixos-hardware raspberry-pi/README.md
deferred Renderer.airplay           -- see: shairport-sync documentation
deferred Renderer.upnp_renderer     -- see: upmpdcli documentation
deferred Websocket.bridge           -- see: websocat documentation
deferred Fleet.rows                 -- see: neoblade-config.allium

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "Whether page-side role limits (decision 8) stay acceptable once the player is used by people outside the household; the upgrade is a filtering proxy between websocat and MPD, which is the backend the decision avoided."
open question "Whether MPD search over a multi-day partial database is useful enough on day one, or whether the guest page should hide search until the first scan completes."
open question "Whether a guest's `play` from the stopped state is welcome at 2 a.m., or whether the host page needs a 'guests may start playback' switch (browser state on the host device, which only the host's page would honour, so again advisory)."
open question "Whether the same file added by two guests should show both names; stickers hold one value per URI, so this needs a different store or a convention such as appending."
open question "Why nixpkgs' online expandOnBoot resize corrupted directory blocks on this card and kernel (linux-rpi 6.18.50, e2fsprogs 1.47.4), and whether it reproduces on a second card; the offline grow is a workaround, not an explanation."
